```js
// Initialize the centralized store, provider, and custom hooks
const { store, Provider, useStateSelectorHook, useDispatchActionHook } =
  manageReactState({
    store: initialStateObject,          // <-- initial state object
    context: reducersMap,               // <-- map of reducer functions
    hooks: { useStateSelectorHook, useDispatchActionHook }, // <-- custom hooks
    middlewares: [loggerMiddleware],   // <-- logger middleware
    enhancers: [applyMiddleware('myMiddleWare')] // <-- enhancer applying your middleware
  });
```

This single line creates:
1. **`store`** – the Redux‑style store holding the global state.  
2. **`Provider`** – a React context provider that makes the store available to the component tree.  
3. **`useStateSelectorHook` & `useDispatchActionHook`** – the custom hooks you’ll use inside components to read state and dispatch actions.  

All configuration (initial state, reducers, middlewares, enhancers) is passed in one object, keeping the initialization concise and maintainable.

